# Intermediate objects emitted by each fixture's build.py.
#
# This rule lives here, matched by pattern, rather than as a copy of the same
# two lines in every fixture directory. Eight of the nine ctest fixtures carried
# that per-directory copy and ctest-ctty did not — so its main.o was committed
# and stayed committed, contradicting the very comment its siblings were
# repeating. A rule replicated per directory is a rule a new directory opts out
# of by simply not having it.
#
# The fastpy fixtures then proved the same point at eleven times the scale: 50
# of the 61 carried a `prog.o` line in their own .gitignore and 11 did not, so
# eleven intermediate objects were tracked. Those 50 files are gone and this
# pattern covers all of them, new directories included.
ctest-*/main.o
fastpy-*/prog.o

# The linked ELFs themselves are ignored at the repository root rather than
# here, next to the note explaining why they stopped being tracked on
# 2026-08-21 (design-decisions.md §355). They are build outputs now: the boot
# test builds what is missing rather than relying on a committed copy, because
# a committed copy links a gitignored libc.a and so goes stale without git
# being able to see it — which it did, in 60 of these 61 directories at once.
